    <briefdescription>
<para>Allows redirection of the output streams cout and cerr from the screen to null (output goes nowhere) and file (ascii file) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Class is used to suppress output on systems where the user has no access to the console and/or where sceen output would dramatically slow the computations.</para>
<para>Only a single stream can be handled by an instance, so return values will reflect that.</para>
<para>Application example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">Mute<sp/>mute;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cout<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;\nMute<sp/>mode...\n&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">mute.Null(cout);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>or<sp/>i.e.<sp/>mute.File(<sp/>cout,<sp/>&quot;Output.txt&quot;);</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...<sp/>here<sp/>goes<sp/>the<sp/>main<sp/>code<sp/>with<sp/>supressed<sp/>output</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">mute.Reinstate(cout);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>a note &apos;just in case&apos;: if you want to supress samg output too, call following for <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_s_a_m_g___settings" kindref="compound">SAMG_Settings</ref> instance (here &apos;settings&apos;) <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">settings.Set_idmp(-1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">settings.Set_iout1(-1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">settings.Set_iout2(-1);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
